      "problem": "Which of the following represents the graph of $y=0.5({9}^{x})?$",
      "worked_solution": "First we plot the graph of $y={9}^{x}$:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194531/assets/270006d7d2e7d7cab172ba586df796af8b78d9b00157f439bf65cc0e151ed13e.png)\n\nThen, we scale this graph vertically by a factor of $0.5.$ The $y$-intercept becomes $(0,0.5),$ and the resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194531/assets/3d0e0db5029b92622d28c478c6a8d3ee02dee21fe3fa1f82965838b22d07f543.png)",
